    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 107.999, 170.607, 504.035, 228.273 ],
    "font" : "SFTI1095",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Proposition 2.13. Let F be a positive integral ∆n-frieze and ﬁx an i ∈ {1,... ,n}. There is a ∆n-frieze F′ corresponding to (x1,... ,xn;y1,... ,yn) ∈ X∆n(N2n) such that F is a horizontal translation of F′ and xi ≤ bi,∆n. Furthermore, if all entries in F are at least 2, then xi ≤ ci,∆n."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 39,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 107.999, 136.407, 503.969, 169.778 ],
    "font" : "SFRM1095",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Proof. Each ∆n-frieze F is a horizontal translation of a frieze F′ in its Z/P∆nZ-orbit such that Fi,1′ ≤ Fi,j′ for all 1 ≤ j ≤ P∆n. By Lemma 2.11, there is a bound on"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 40,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 119.519, 119.007, 188.453, 141.338 ],
    "font" : "EURM10",
    "font size" : 7.97,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "P∆n j=1 Fi,j′ ≤ bPi,∆∆n"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 42,
    "level" : "3",
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 107.999, 85.847, 503.964, 139.418 ],
    "font" : "SFRM1095",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : ". But xi = Fi,1′ is the smallest factor in the product of P∆n-many terms, hence xi ≤ bi,∆n. If the entries of F are all at least 2, then the entries of the translation F′ are also all at least 2. Hence the same argument gives the bound in terms of ci,∆n instead of bi,∆n."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 41,
